+# SG-2026-07-30-06 — Status-aware publication safety
+
+SG-06 supersedes SG-05 append-preservingly after the public website moved from broad recursive repository copying to an explicit, default-exclude publication constitution.
+
+The transition makes only the publication-control layer canonical:
+
+```text
+default publication decision:              exclude
+recursive repository copy:                  false
+unclassified dependency allowed:             false
+generic graph.json public route:              false
+legacy/ public route:                         false
+primary public atlas:              surface-hop only
+POOF status:                     staged_nonpublic
+POOF GitHub Pages deployment:                 false
+SSC publication status:                    blocked
+publication manifest:              exact-byte required
+graph effect:                                 none
+```
+
+The checkpoint does not establish source truth, coordination, POOF deployment, DCA prevalence, field effect, adoption, or authority to conduct a real-person pilot. K0 remains 9/9 with zero included events; DCA execution remains 0/12; maximum verified adoption remains A0.
